---
import Icon from '../Icon.astro';
import Button from '../Button.astro';
---

<section class="flex items-center overflow-clip bg-cream py-section lg:h-[55.125rem]">
	<!-- 2x2 grid: title sits in column 1 / row 1, the supporting copy in
	     column 2 / row 2, leaving the opposite corners empty. -->
	<div
		class="container-large grid w-full grid-cols-1 gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-rows-2 lg:gap-16"
	>
		<div class="flex flex-col gap-6 lg:col-start-1 lg:row-start-1">
			<Icon name="globe" class="h-12 w-12 shrink-0" tint />
			<h2 class="display text-[2.25rem] leading-[1.1] text-ink lg:text-h2" data-anim="text">
				<span class="text-ink/40">Here&rsquo;s an opportunity on the table. </span>
				Do you already know what security will win you?
			</h2>
		</div>

		<div class="flex flex-col justify-end gap-6 lg:col-start-2 lg:row-start-2">
			<p
				class="text-xl font-medium leading-[1.3] tracking-[-0.03em] text-graphite lg:text-h4"
				data-anim="text"
			>
				If the answer to that question is no: no shame. All of this is new — the
				laws, the geopolitical situation, AI. There IS no best practice yet, and no
				expert who can explain it all. Nobody has done this before.
			</p>
			<Button href="#apply" variant="blue" class="w-fit" label="Apply to join →" />
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
